# Understanding the Query

Micrometer exposes two important heap metrics.

The first metric is:

```promql
jvm_memory_used_bytes
```

This represents the amount of heap currently occupied by Java objects.

---

The second metric is:

```promql
jvm_memory_max_bytes
```

This represents the maximum heap available to the JVM.

---

The query calculates:

```
Current Heap Usage

———————————————

Maximum Heap Size
```

Result:

```
0

↓

1
```

Example

```
Heap Used

512 MB

Maximum Heap

1024 MB

Result

0.50

=

50%
```

---

# Why Use sum()

Modern Spring Boot applications may run multiple Pods.

Each Pod exposes its own JVM metrics.

Using:

```promql
sum(...)
/
sum(...)
```

aggregates heap utilization across all running Pods.

This provides a single operational metric representing the entire platform.

