# Verification

Generate application traffic.

Example:

```
Refresh

https://api.dev.dreammyles.online/actuator/health

multiple times
```

Observe the JVM Heap gauge.

Heap utilization should increase as objects are allocated.

After Garbage Collection,

heap utilization should decrease.

This "saw-tooth" pattern is expected behavior.

---

# Understanding Heap Behavior

Unlike CPU utilization,

heap memory does not always decrease immediately.

A healthy JVM often displays a repeating pattern.

```
20%

↓

35%

↓

48%

↓

62%

↓

GC Runs

↓

28%

↓

42%

↓

57%

↓

GC Runs

↓

30%
```

This repeating increase and decrease indicates that Garbage Collection is functioning correctly.

If heap utilization continually increases without decreasing,

a memory leak may exist.

